      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright 2014, SLACK Incorporated.",
        "AbstractText": "Childhood overweight and obesity is a major health concern in the United States. It is recommended that every well-child examination include body mass index measurements and obesity prevention discussions that encourage healthy eating habits, regular physical exercise, and limited television and computer screen time. Providers can make a difference through strategic intervention."
